{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8d4f5a2e-6c91-4b73-a2d8-1f0e9c7b3a65",
    "name": "encryption-services (crypto-api)",
    "description": "crypto-api listens on container port 2796 over TLS 1.3 with mTLS (RequireAndVerifyClientCert). Compose maps 127.0.0.1:2896 to 2796 by default; set CRYPTO_API_PORT to change the host port. The client certificate CN must be `app` (default APP_IDENTITIES), or the API returns 403 {\"fault\":{\"code\":403,\"message\":\"forbidden\"}}.\n\nClient certificate setup: Postman Settings > Certificates > Add certificate. Host: 127.0.0.1:2896. CRT file: `cryptography-service/run/pki/api/app-cert.pem`, KEY file: `cryptography-service/run/pki/api/app-cert-key.pem` (the same CN `app` client cert the backend uses, see root compose.yaml CRYPTO_CERT/CRYPTO_KEY). Treat app-cert-key.pem as a secret: never commit or share it. Under CA Certificates add `run/pki/api/ca.pem` (relative to `cryptography-service/`). `run/pki/api/crypto-api.pem` and `run/pki/api/crypto-api-key.pem` are server-side, not for Postman. SSL verification may need to be off if the server certificate SAN does not include 127.0.0.1.\n\ncrypto-api is stateless. DEKs come from keyd over a Unix socket. Requests carry no key or DEK field. Ciphertexts embed `t1:<dek_id>` issued by keyd. All API routes are POST with JSON bodies and JSON responses. Errors use {\"fault\":{\"code\":<int>,\"message\":\"<string>\"}}. Validation errors are 400 (code 1066, message starts `INVALID_JSON_REQUEST: `); crypto/input errors are 501; key zone unavailability is 503 with message `KEY_UNAVAILABLE: kunci enkripsi tidak dapat digunakan (DEK/KEK tidak tersedia dari key zone). Operasi enkripsi/dekripsi gagal. Cek koneksi ke keyd dan layanan TPM di DMZ.`; audit unavailability is 503 with message `audit unavailable`. No auth header or query parameters.\n\nThe separate internal listener is plain HTTP on :2797 (default CRYPTO_INTERNAL_ADDR), not published by compose. Its GET /internal/traffic request is listed separately and needs the container port exposed.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
